---
title: Beef stew
servings: 6
tags: [american, beef, braise, one-pot, winter]
cuisine: american
time: 4 hours
source: Beef Stew by Jennifer Segal, Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/beef-stew-with-carrots-potatoes.html
---

Heat the oven to 325°F (165°C) with a rack in the lower middle.

Pat the @beef chuck{3%lb}(boneless, in 1 1/2-inch pieces) dry and season with
@salt{2%tsp} and @black pepper{1%tsp}(freshly ground).

Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a #Dutch oven{} over medium-high heat. Brown the beef
in three batches, ~{5%minutes} each, adding @olive oil{2%tbsp} a tablespoon at a
time between batches. Set the meat aside on a plate.

Add the @yellow onions{2}(in 1-inch chunks), @garlic{7%cloves}(smashed) and
@balsamic vinegar{2%tbsp}. Cook ~{5%minutes}, scraping up the browned bits. Stir
in the @tomato paste{1.5%tbsp} and cook ~{1%minute}.

Return the beef and its juices, sprinkle over the @all-purpose flour{1/4%cup},
and stir ~{2%minutes} until it disappears.

Add the @red wine{2%cup}(dry), @beef broth{2%cup}, @water{2%cup}, @bay leaf{1},
@dried thyme{1/2%tsp} and @sugar{1.5%tsp}. Stir, bring to a boil, cover, and
braise in the oven ~{2%hours}.

Add the @carrots{4}(large, in 1-inch diagonal chunks) and
@potatoes{1%lb}(small boiling, halved). Cover and return to the oven ~{1%hour},
until the vegetables are cooked and the meat is tender.

Take out the bay leaf, season to taste, and scatter with @parsley{}(chopped).

> Without an oven-safe pot, simmer it covered on the lowest heat for the same
> time.
